# ── NEAR-TIP reflection seed — REGENERATE AT DEPLOY TIME (these are a STALE @958735 example, do NOT ship as-is) ──
# The resume digest + anchor are IMMUTABLE and must be a MATCHED pair for the SAME reflected state:
#   REFLECTION_RESUME_DIGEST = idx.digest(the head snapshot the worker will be seeded with)
#   GENESIS_REFLECTION_ANCHOR = that snapshot's matured tip = relay.tip() walked back 6, LITTLE-ENDIAN internal
# A mismatched pair bricks the first attest (StaleReflectionDigest/UnanchoredReflection) on an immutable pool;
# a far-behind anchor forces a large first fold (the big-batch OOM trap). The relay advances ~every 10 min, so
# this MUST be recomputed right before broadcast, not reused. Procedure:
#   1. tools/reflection-regen-verify.mjs — fold the saved head snapshot forward to the current matured tip,
#      stopping when its newDigest matches; it writes tools/.regen/head-snapshot.json ONLY on a verified match.
#   2. Set REFLECTION_RESUME_DIGEST = that snapshot's digest, GENESIS_REFLECTION_ANCHOR = its matured tip (LE).
#   3. DeployV1SuiteCreateX staticcalls relay.blockHeight(anchor) != 0 (byte-order guard); confirm the anchor
#      height is within a few blocks of relay best height (fresh) before broadcasting.
#   4. POST-DEPLOY: seed the worker with the SAME head-snapshot.json via tools/seed-reflection-head.mjs.
export REFLECTION_RESUME_DIGEST=  # <-- fill from step 1 (empty ⇒ deploy would fall back to full-history replay: DO NOT ship empty on a resume)
export GENESIS_REFLECTION_ANCHOR=  # <-- fill from step 2 (matured tip, little-endian internal hash)
# Stale @958735 example (relay tip 958741-6; superseded — kept only as a format reference):
#   REFLECTION_RESUME_DIGEST=0x0df5dd17e0ce85e8087d093d41fd9057bdadcf281d3bd642239373a097ee5c83
#   GENESIS_REFLECTION_ANCHOR=0x52bb4d1f23a2f5260cb08cf57c147da86d3a1473abee01000000000000000000

